asr(3, 'loss', 'The introduction of the Nile perch led to loss of cichlid fishes in Lake Victoria.', 'The Nile perch is a predator of the cichlids.', 0, 'The predator fed on the endemic cichlids and eliminated more than 200 species.');
asr(3, 'conservation', 'Sacred groves protect biodiversity.', 'The people there protect the forest patches on religious grounds.', 0, 'The belief keeps trees and animals untouched, so biodiversity is protected.');
asr(3, 'importance', 'Plant-pollinator relations show the importance of biodiversity.', 'Pollinators like bees, birds and bats are needed for plant reproduction.', 0, 'This is a broadly utilitarian value, as the plants can\'t produce fruit without the pollinators.');
stm(3, 'patterns', 'Species richness increases from the poles towards the equator.', 'Greenland has more bird species than Colombia.', 2, 'Colombia has nearly 1400 species; Greenland only 56. Statement II is false.');
stm(3, 'loss', 'Introduction of alien species is a cause of loss of biodiversity.', 'Water hyacinth is an alien invasive weed.', 0, 'Both are correct.');
stm(3, 'conservation', 'Cryopreservation uses liquid nitrogen at -196 °C.', 'Cryopreservation is an in situ method.', 2, 'It is an ex situ method. Statement II is false.');
