mc(5, 'levels', 'India has about 45,000 plant species. The textbook says the number of animal species is about', 'twice that of plants', ['half of that of plants', 'one tenth of plants', 'the same as plants'], 'India has about 45,000 plant species and nearly twice as many animal species, so its share of 8.1 per cent of the world species is high.');
mc(5, 'patterns', 'A student finds that species richness on islands of 10 km<sup>2</sup> and 1000 km<sup>2</sup> differ. If Z is 0.2, the larger island has', '2.5 times as many species', ['100 times as many', '10 times as many', '20 times as many'], '(1000/10)<sup>0.2</sup> = 100<sup>0.2</sup> = 2.51.');
mc(5, 'patterns', 'Which of the following correctly states the meaning of C in log S = log C + Z log A?', 'The Y-intercept of the straight line', ['The slope', 'The area', 'The number of species at zero area'], 'C is the intercept; Z is the slope.', 'Do not confuse the intercept with the slope.');
mc(5, 'importance', 'Which is TRUE of the statement "out of every 10 animals on the planet 7 are insects"?', 'Insects make up over 70 per cent of animal species', ['Insects are 7 per cent of animals', 'Insects are 70 per cent of plants', 'It is a statement on biomass'], 'This is about species numbers, not mass or individuals.', 'Species count, not individual count.');
mc(5, 'importance', 'A drug company collects plants from the forest of a country and makes a drug without sharing the benefit. This is', 'biopiracy and an issue linked to bioprospecting', ['conservation', 'cryopreservation', 'speciation'], 'Bioprospecting without authorisation and benefit sharing is biopiracy.');
mc(5, 'loss', 'Which statement correctly identifies a species lost by an alien invasion rather than by hunting?', 'Cichlid fishes of Lake Victoria', ['Passenger pigeon', 'Steller\'s sea cow', 'Dodo'], 'The cichlids went because of the Nile perch.');
mc(5, 'loss', 'Over the past 500 years, the numbers of extinct invertebrates, vertebrates and plants recorded are 338, 359 and 87. Which statement is correct?', 'Vertebrates were the largest of the three groups recorded', ['Plants were the largest group', 'Invertebrates were the smallest group', 'All were equal'], '359 vertebrates > 338 invertebrates > 87 plants.');
mc(5, 'conservation', 'Which of these does NOT happen in a biosphere reserve or sanctuary?', 'Complete removal of the species to a zoo', ['Legal protection of the area', 'Protection of habitat and wildlife', 'Conservation in the natural habitat'], 'These are in situ areas and do not remove species from the habitat.');
mc(5, 'conservation', 'The best reason to conserve hotspots first is that', 'they have many endemic species that are under severe threat, so the gain per unit area is highest', ['they are large', 'they have no humans', 'they are in the tropics only'], 'Hotspots make up a small area but protect a large share of the species at risk.');
mc(5, 'conservation', 'Which pair is correct for ex situ conservation?', 'Gametes of threatened species: cryopreservation in liquid nitrogen', ['Sacred grove: botanical garden', 'Wildlife sanctuary: seed bank', 'National park: zoo'], 'Gametes can be stored in liquid nitrogen at -196 °C.');
asr(5, 'patterns', 'On a log-log plot, the species-area relationship is a straight line.', 'The relationship is S = C A<sup>Z</sup>, so log S is linear in log A.', 0, 'Taking logs of both sides gives a linear form with slope Z.');
asr(5, 'importance', 'A community with more species is more stable.', 'Tilman showed that biomass of species-rich plots varies less from year to year.', 0, 'The experiment supports the idea.');
asr(5, 'loss', 'The number of extinctions in the past was lower than in the present.', 'The present extinction rate is 100 to 1000 times higher than the natural rate.', 0, 'The sixth extinction is much faster, so more species are lost now.');
stm(5, 'loss', 'Aliens can be a cause of loss of native species.', 'Native species are not harmed by invasive species.', 2, 'Invasive species harm native species through competition and predation.');
stm(5, 'patterns', 'A larger Z means species richness rises more steeply with area.', 'Z for continents is lower than for small regions.', 2, 'Z for continents (0.6-1.2) is higher than for small regions (0.1-0.2).');
mc(5, 'conservation', 'How many of the following are in situ conservation: sacred grove, botanical garden, seed bank, biosphere reserve, zoological park, national park?', 'Three', ['Two', 'Four', 'Five'], 'Sacred grove, biosphere reserve and national park are in situ. The other three are ex situ.', null, 'statements');
mc(5, 'patterns', 'How many of the following are correct about the tropics? (a) Less seasonal. (b) Undisturbed for millions of years. (c) More solar energy. (d) Frequent glaciation.', 'Three', ['Two', 'Four', 'One'], '(a), (b) and (c) are correct. (d) applies to temperate regions.', 'Glaciation belongs to the temperate side.', 'statements');
match(5, 'importance', 'xm7', 'Argument for conservation and example', ['A. Narrowly utilitarian', 'B. Broadly utilitarian', 'C. Ethical', 'D. Bioprospecting'], ['p. Drugs from plants', 'q. Oxygen from the Amazon', 'r. Every species has intrinsic value', 's. Exploring for products of economic importance'], 'A-p, B-q, C-r, D-s', ['A-q, B-p, C-r, D-s', 'A-p, B-q, C-s, D-r', 'A-r, B-q, C-p, D-s'], 'Direct use is narrowly utilitarian, services are broadly utilitarian, intrinsic value is ethical and bioprospecting explores for products.');
match(5, 'conservation', 'xm8', 'Summit and what it did', ['A. Rio de Janeiro 1992', 'B. Johannesburg 2002', 'C. IUCN Red List', 'D. Hotspot'], ['p. Called on nations to conserve biodiversity and use it sustainably', 'q. 190 countries pledged to reduce biodiversity loss by 2010', 'r. List of threatened species', 's. High species richness and endemism under threat'], 'A-p, B-q, C-r, D-s', ['A-q, B-p, C-r, D-s', 'A-p, B-q, C-s, D-r', 'A-r, B-q, C-p, D-s'], 'Rio set the call, Johannesburg a pledge, the Red List records threatened species and a hotspot has richness and endemism.');
nat(5, 'loss', 'Of 784 recorded extinctions over the last 500 years, 87 are plants. What percentage are plants? Give one decimal.', 11.1, '87/784 × 100 = 11.097, about 11.1 per cent.', '%', 'Divide by the total (784).', 0.05);

